cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or reference this specification, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Decision-Sequence Evidence Schema (DSES)"
abstract: >-
  An open, vendor-neutral vocabulary for evidence of how humans and AI
  make decisions together. DSES defines a ten-event vocabulary for
  human-AI decision sequences, an eight-class exposure ontology, an
  information-state and independence model, four integrity classes, and
  three conformance levels, with mappings to HL7 FHIR AuditEvent and
  Provenance, IHE Radiology AI profiles, DICOM, and OpenTelemetry.
